nds much of his time behind the  camera after graduating from Chapman  University with a degree in Film  Production he co-founded LP Studios a  production and post-production Company  for the film and music Industries his  work includes everything from sound  mixing to cinematography  David kromholtz's screen acting career  was just beginning when he landed the  role of Bernard he's the grumpy but  ultimately compassionate head elf who  guides Scots and Charlie through their  North Pole journey and ultimately  provides a way for the father and son to  stay in contact at the end of the film  krumholtz's acting career gained  considerable steam throughout the 1990s  and 2000s so much so that while he  reprized his role for the Santa Claus 2  he was unable to return for The Santa  Clause 3 The Escape Clause because of  another commitment  where'd he go  that commitment was krumholtz's other  best known role mathematician Charlie  Epps on the hit CBS drama numbers a role  he played for five years and nearly 120  episodes to this day grumholtz continues  to work regularly in both film and  television more recently appearing in  the TV series living biblically and the  deuce and films like The Ballad of  Buster Scruggs  and acclaimed talent in the United  States as well as her native Canada  Wendy crewson worked regularly  throughout the 1980s in film and  television and she landed the role of  Laura Miller in the Santa Claus like her  frequent scene partner Judge Reinhold  she grew from non-believer to supporter  and Ally and Scott Calvin's Santa  adventures and the film's popularity  allowed her to return for both of its  sequels crewson also continued to work  regularly after the Santa Claus and  gained higher profile roles in American  film and television because of it among  her other major credits after the film  are Air Force One starring Harrison Ford  and the Canadian Supernatural medical  drama Saving Hope in which she  co-starred for Five Seasons between 2012  